To incorporate the STOR and SITE commands into the sequence of client requests while maintaining the logical flow of FTP commands, we can add the STOR command after the LIST command and the SITE command before the QUIT command. Here'ypically used in conjunction with `RNFR` to rename a file on the server.

Here is a modified sequence that CWDincludes `RETR` and `RNTO` commands:

```
USER ubuntu
PASS ubuntu
SYST
PWD
PORT 1RNTO,0,1,132,209
LIST
MKD test
RETR filename.txt    ; (Assuming we want to retrieve a file named filename.txt)
RNFR oldname.txt     ; (Assuming we want ty rename oldname.txt)
RNTO newname.txt     ; (Renaming oldname.txt to newname.txt)
QUIT
```

